# Austin A30/A35 two-door saloon, 1951-1962.
#
# The "New Austin Seven": 3,467 mm long, 1,422 mm wide, 1,505 mm high,
# 2,032 mm wheelbase; 803 cc A-series four. The A35 of 1956 brought a larger rear
# window and a painted grille. One shell covers both; the model represents the
# A30 with the chrome grille.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin_A30
#
# Colours: Black, Grey, Blue and Green are documented Austin colours of the
# period.
#
# Weight: 200 in total (black 70, grey 50, blue 45, green 35).
#
# Speed 100 km/h; comfort 40/240 (line). Classes 0,1.
# Dates: 1951-1962 with a road tail to about 1978.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/austin-a30.blend. References:
# citycars/references/austin-a30/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=AustinA30(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=70
intro_year=1951
intro_month=10
retire_year=1978
retire_month=6
speed=100
class=0,1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=40
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=240

